  "body": "AGENTS.md (\"Use the gh-issues skill\", added in 57ae394e), `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/classify-effort/SKILL.md` and `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md` all tell agents to load the `gh-issues` skill first, but the skill isn't in the repo (`git ls-tree upstream/main -- .claude/skills` has no `gh-issues`). It appears to live only in the maintainer's personal `~/.claude/skills/`. Every other session (forks, other machines) gets `Unknown skill: gh-issues` and falls back to raw `gh`.\n\nDone means: `.claude/skills/gh-issues/SKILL.md` is committed (the gh mechanics: list limits, search syntax, heredoc bodies, closing keywords, `--repo` for fork work), `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is bumped, and #681 is announced, so the process-file sync carries it to every fork. Alternative: drop the references if the skill is meant to stay personal.\n\nOnly the maintainer has the skill's text, so this isn't for an agent to write from scratch.\n",
